  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Piedicavallo Tarocchi. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Piedicavallo Tarocchi is a rare and highly localized variant of Italian Tarot played exclusively in the Valle Cervo of the Piedmont region. It uses a modified 62-card 'Tarocco Piemontese' deck. The game is famous for its 'Open Communication' system, where partners are legally allowed to speak to each other and signal their cards (using taps and code words) as long as the information is audible to the opponents. It is a game of deep tactical coordination, memory, and traditional heritage.",
    objective: 'Score 57 or more points from a pool of 114 available points.',
    gameplay: "Four players in fixed partnerships (partners opposite) play four deals anticlockwise. Each deal: dealer gives 15 cards to the player to his right, 15 to partner, 15 to the player to his left, and 17 to himself; dealer then discards two cards face-down (scarto). Player to dealer's right leads to the first trick. Follow suit if possible; if not, play a trump if possible; otherwise play any card. Trick with trumps is won by highest trump; trick without trumps by highest card of led suit. Winner of each trick leads to the next. The Fool may be played to any trick and never wins; it is added to the team of whoever played it. Team with more than 57 of the 114 points over the four deals wins the game.",
    keyRules: [
      'Follow suit if possible; if void in suit led, must play a trump if possible.',
      'Fool may be played to any trick; it never wins and is not captured; it counts for the team of the player who played it.',
      'Dealer may not discard 5-point cards (Kings, Trump 21, Trump 1, Fool).',
      '57 or more points of 114 wins a deal; team ahead on total points after four deals wins the game.',
      'Partners may communicate about their cards and tactics within defined limits (open communication).',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: true,
